SWTOR on Mac: native fullscreen (NativeFullscreen, off unless the registry turns it on; SWTOR on
Mac turns it on for swtor.exe with "Native fullscreen (own Space)" in Settings).

When the game's borderless window covers one screen, the driver moves it into a fullscreen
Space of its own (toggleFullScreen: on the borderless window with FullScreenPrimary, which
AppKit takes on macOS 27, #118) and takes it out when it stops qualifying. With the option off
no new code path runs.

- One decision (plain C at the top of cocoa_window.m, tested by scripts/test-nativefs-decide.sh): every event
  records the window's facts and asks it; only it starts a transition. A window qualifies when
  it is top-level, shown, not minimized, disabled or maximized, borderless as Wine last asked,
  its requested content covers exactly one screen (within a point) or equals the content of the
  Space it is in, the displays aren't captured, the player hasn't left this Space by hand, and
  "Displays have separate Spaces" is on or one screen is attached. It enters after 300 ms of
  qualifying, with the app active and the window on the active Space; it leaves after 150 ms of
  not qualifying, or for a request on another screen (then enters there). A failed entry backs
  off 2 s, 3 tries at most; a failed exit is retried once after 1 s. A real display change
  holds everything for 1 s.
- In the Space AppKit owns the frame: Wine's frame and style requests are recorded, not
  applied. Where the Space's content differs from the request (a notch), Wine is told the real
  frame once per request; more than 3 such corrections in 2 s leave the Space ("fight") and keep
  it left. On the way out the pending style applies first, then the frame of Wine's latest
  request; the frame saved at entry is never posted to Wine.
- Quiet transitions: for a transition the driver started (or took over from the player's own
  entry of the game's window), no resize-start query, no min/max query, no resize-ended event,
  no frames while AppKit animates, and frame posts without the size-move pair. The main thread
  never waits for the game's window thread during them.
- The player's exit (the Window menu, the shortcut) wins: the window stays out until it stops
  qualifying or the player enters again by hand.
- In the Space: FullScreen|HideDock|HideMenuBar, the normal window level, FullScreenPrimary kept
  while the window qualifies or is in the Space. After each transition the next mouse move is
  absolute, relative mouse mode is decided again and a cursor clip is set again. Raw mouse-look
  doesn't end for a window in a transition the driver started (it is briefly off the active
  Space then).
- Debug output: warn+nativefs, the NATIVEFS lines (on, enter, entered, exit reason=, exited,
  resize told wine=, enter failed, exit failed, stuck, declined by user, fight, skipped).

